// GuardStability: is the HC guard loop stable with the electrodes in air (SPEC.md,
// "Guard loop stability")? The circuit of PumpOutputImpedance: the drive at 0 V,
// the HC strays of SoilSweep (20 pF from the node to its guard, 0.3 pF to ground,
// 100 pF from the guard to the ground layer), nothing else on E_HC; the test
// current source is at 0 A, so it is open.
//
// The poles settle it: none in the right half-plane. The least damped pair is at
// 4.06 kHz with damping 0.27 and dominates DRIVE, U_PMP and the guard: the pump,
// its DC servo C_NDC and the guard feeding the node back. It is the 45 Mohm
// resonance of PumpOutputImpedance's output impedance, which peaks at 4.07 kHz
// with a half-power width of 3.13 to 5.25 kHz, Q 1.9, damping 0.26 (an ac sweep
// from 10 Hz; that bench starts at 1 kHz). The three poles at the origin are the
// electrode nodes E_HP and E_LP, which in air connect through capacitors only.
//
// The loop gain at the guard resistor's input (R_GHC.1) is reported without a
// limit and is not a stability margin: that break is two-way (the pump's own
// positive feedback through R2 returns to the guard as well as the guard to the
// pump), so Tian's loop gain there is not the return ratio of one loop; it shows
// 2.5 degrees of "phase margin" where the poles show damping 0.27. The margins at
// the amplifiers' outputs, one-way breaks, are limited as in LoopStability.
bench GuardStability for AnalogFrontEnd using FrontEndPorts {
    model DDS: source { out = DDS_OUT; ref = GND; ac = 0V; output_resistance = 200ohm; }   // drive held at 0 V
    replace J_PROBE with source { out = E_HC; ref = GND; output = current; ac = 0A; }   // open: electrodes in air

    component CG_HC: CAPACITOR { value = 20pF; }
    component C0_HC: CAPACITOR { value = 0.3pF; }
    component GG_HC: CAPACITOR { value = 100pF; }
    net E_HC { CG_HC.1; C0_HC.1; }
    net GUARD_HC { CG_HC.2; GG_HC.1; }
    net GND { C0_HC.2; GG_HC.2; }

    // The built-in measure stable fails when a pole is in the right half-plane.
    analysis poles: pz;
    measure damping = damping();

    analysis pump: loop { from = 10Hz; to = 10GHz; points_per_decade = 40; probe = U_PMP.OUT; }
    measure phase_margin = phase_margin(loop_gain()) { min = 45deg; }
    measure crossover = crossover(loop_gain());

    analysis feedback_buffer: loop { from = 10Hz; to = 10GHz; points_per_decade = 40; probe = U_FBB.OUT; }
    measure phase_margin = phase_margin(loop_gain()) { min = 45deg; }
    measure crossover = crossover(loop_gain());

    analysis guard_resistor: loop { from = 10Hz; to = 10GHz; points_per_decade = 40; probe = R_GHC.1; }
    measure largest_gain = max(mag(loop_gain()));
    measure crossover = crossover(loop_gain());
    measure apparent_phase_margin = phase_margin(loop_gain());
}
